{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Who acquit.</b> And the wine blinds their heart; also the bribe blinds their heart." "<b>Because of.</b> On account of, like the sense of שכר באחרונה, from the root of ואת עקבו מים (Joshua 8:13)." "<b>And the righteousness of.</b> Every one of the righteous they remove from it, like בנות צעדה עלי שור (Genesis 49:22)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra identifies עקב here with the root meaning 'heel/end,' glossed via שכר באחרונה; the comparison to Joshua 8:13 (where עקב means 'rear') is left as he gives it.", 2 "The quoted phrase from Genesis 49:22 uses צעדה (= stepped/trod), supporting his reading of the verb in Isaiah as 'remove/trample away'; rendered exactly as he cites it."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:59.381442469Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}